# ── ROM content: never committed, in any form (CLAUDE.md §2 rule 7) ──────────
# Reference sets live OUTSIDE the tree in $ROMDIR; these patterns are defense
# in depth in case anything ROM-shaped ever lands inside the repo.
*.zip
*.7z
*.bin
*.rom
*.key
# CPS-2 part-number naming (vsav/vsav2/vhunt2 program, gfx, qsound files)
vm3*.*
vs2*.*
vh2*.*
*.03[a-e]
*.04[a-e]
*.[0-9][0-9]m
dl-1425*
# Decrypted / intermediate ROM images
build/out/
build/cache/
*.decrypted
*.prg

# ── Emulator working dirs and artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
# emu/fbneo is a git submodule (gitlink only; its content is never committed here)
emu/*/build/
cfg/
nvram/
diff/
inp/
snap/
sta/
mame.ini
ui.ini
plugin.ini

# ── Tooling noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
re/ghidra/*
!re/ghidra/.keep
!re/ghidra/README.md

# ── OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*

# ── Exceptions: savestates/replays that tests depend on are force-added ──────
# (git add -f, per CLAUDE.md savestate hygiene; no blanket un-ignore here)
build/donovan/

# Generated CPS-2 WIDE romset overlays: directories of ABSOLUTE symlinks into
# $ROMDIR plus one clone zip, rebuilt in one command (HANDOFF). Tracking them
# put a stale absolute symlink in git, which dangled the moment the repo path
# changed and produced a false gate FAIL (14z-61, docs/GOTCHAS.md).
build/wide0/rompath/
build/wide_canary/rompath/
build/manifest/probe_*.toml
build/probe_*/
build/probe_*.log

# ── 14z-91 (GitHub #39/#40, maintainer-ruled) ────────────────────────────
# WIDE extension program members. `vsw.*`, NOT `vsw*.*`: the pattern must
# not also swallow authored sources that happen to start with those letters.
# Measured today these are 0xFF fill (12 of 16 a single repeated byte), so
# the audit's "8 MiB of ROM-derived output" was false — but the profile
# targets ~338 KB of PORTED PROGRAM ROM landing in exactly these members,
# and rule 7 is about what the repo will hold tomorrow, not today.
vsw.*

# Root-anchored build/clone trees that were never meant to be committed.
# The worktrees entry is not cosmetic: 471 MB of duplicated tools/tests/docs
# under .claude/worktrees/ makes every retraction-discipline grep return
# pre-move copies, so a session can "fix" a claim in a worktree and believe
# it done (paid for repeatedly in 14z-90 and again in 14z-91 — every grep in
# this repo now needs `| grep -v worktrees`). Scoped to .claude/worktrees/,
# NOT a blanket .claude/, so agent/skill config stays trackable.
/fbneo/
/mame/
/.claude/worktrees/
